# N21 independent substantive choice review

Outcome: **REVISE**, not PASS. Mechanical checks passed on the first native
validator invocation; exit 3 preserves the nonpassing semantic review.

## Finding

Exercise 428 / q07 has an undeclared assessment loss. Every A/B/C option supplies
the identical correct original five-point graph. A learner can therefore skip
reading the source arrows, use that supplied graph, reverse its coordinates, and
decide functionhood. The inverse task is still substantive and mathematically
correct, but the intent claims "Read all five actual arrows" while the limitations
and coverage declare only the loss of plotting both graphs. They do not declare
that original arrow-to-point inference is supplied and unassessed.

Either explicitly declare that assessment loss and narrow the intent/coverage
claim, or make original-graph interpretation discriminate candidates. This is
scoped to 428/q07, not a demand to recreate figures or reject complete-locus
recognition. The draft was not edited.

## Mathematics and scope

All 11 sources were independently solved before the candidate projection.
All 23 visible questions and all 93 options were independently checked and frozen
before intent, rationales or keys were opened. Every complete true set and every
per-option truth agrees with the author; every distractor's declared wrong
procedure was compared against its actual mathematical result. All other source
coverage checks pass, with declared writing/drawing-to-recognition limitations.

For 431, diameter-endpoint membership remains **UNKNOWN**. q10 explicitly excludes
that judgment and retains the complete right arc away from those endpoints.
The inverse points (1,+sqrt8) and (1,-sqrt8) prove nonfunction independently of the
endpoint convention. Thus endpoint membership is not an essential missing
condition for q10, and does not block it or unrelated sources. A fully
endpoint-specified graph is still deferred, not approved.

## Figure observation

Exactly two actual images were opened in one batch, without reopens or inherited
payloads: source fig-41.png and the prepared complete fig-41.svg.png. Both visibly
show left nodes -2,-1,1,3,4, right nodes -2,-1,1, and arrows
-2->1, -1->-1, 1->-2, 3->-1, 4->1. The bottommost/rightmost objects and complete
set boundaries were visible. Crossings are not vertices. Figure owner is 428,
not 435. Existing figure PASS is reused; no FigureSpec, rerender, validate_spec or
full figure review was performed.

